• Path Manipulation (Paths.get(), Path.resolve(), Path.normalize())
Defines hierarchical file or directory paths without accessing the file system directly.

• File Operations (Files.copy(), Files.move(), Files.delete())
Performs file system tasks and accepts CopyOption flags like REPLACE_EXISTING.

• Streaming File Content (Files.lines(Path))
Reads lines lazily as a Stream<String> to prevent high memory use on large files.

• Directory Streams (Files.list(Path))
Returns a Stream<Path> listing entries of a single directory level.

• Recursive Traversal (Files.walk(Path))
Recursively traverses a directory tree using depth-first search.

• Attribute Matching (Files.find(Path, depth, BiPredicate))
Filters path tree entries using built-in file attributes like BasicFileAttributes.
